## 1. Create a Student Class Using a Parameterized Constructor

### 💡 Concept

A constructor is a special member of a class used to initialize an object.

- Its name must match the class name.
- It has no return type, not even `void`.
- A parameterized constructor accepts values when an object is created.

### 💻 Code

```java
class Student {
    String name;
    int age;

    Student(String name, int age) {
        this.name = name;
        this.age = age;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Student s = new Student("Rahul", 21);

        System.out.println("Name: " + s.name);
        System.out.println("Age: " + s.age);
    }
}
```

### 📤 Output

```text
Name: Rahul
Age: 21
```

### 🧠 Memory Trick

**Constructor = Initial setup of an object.**

`this.name` refers to the object's field, while `name` refers to the constructor parameter.

