## 2. Create Two Student Objects Using the Same Constructor

### 💡 Concept

One class can create many objects. Each object can store different values in its instance variables.

### 💻 Code

```java
class Student {
    String name;
    int age;

    Student(String name, int age) {
        this.name = name;
        this.age = age;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Student s1 = new Student("Rahul", 21);
        Student s2 = new Student("Priya", 20);

        System.out.println("Name: " + s1.name);
        System.out.println("Age: " + s1.age);

        System.out.println("Name: " + s2.name);
        System.out.println("Age: " + s2.age);
    }
}
```

### 📤 Output

```text
Name: Rahul
Age: 21
Name: Priya
Age: 20
```

### 🧠 Memory Trick

**One class → Many objects → Different data.**

