## 4. Display Student Name Using an Instance Variable

### 💡 Concept

An instance variable belongs to an object. An instance method can directly access the instance variables of the same object.

### 💻 Code

```java
class Student {
    String name;

    void displayName() {
        System.out.println("Student Name: " + name);
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Student s = new Student();
        s.name = "Rahul";
        s.displayName();
    }
}
```

### 📤 Output

```text
Student Name: Rahul
```

### 🧠 Memory Trick

- `s.name = "Rahul";` stores a value.
- `s.displayName();` calls the method.
- `name` inside the instance method refers to the current object's field.

