## 6. Check Passing Grade Using an Instance Variable

### 💡 Concept

The `if-else` statement allows a program to choose between two paths based on a condition.

Here, marks of 35 or above mean Pass.

### 💻 Code

```java
class StudentGrade {
    int marks;

    void checkResult() {
        if (marks >= 35) {
            System.out.println("Pass");
        } else {
            System.out.println("Fail");
        }
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        StudentGrade s = new StudentGrade();
        s.marks = 72;
        s.checkResult();
    }
}
```

### 📤 Output

```text
Pass
```

### 🧠 Memory Trick

- `if` → condition is true.
- `else` → condition is false.
- `>=` → greater than or equal to.

