## 8. Calculate the Square of a Number Using an Instance Method

### 💡 Concept

The square of a number is the number multiplied by itself.

Formula: `square = number * number`

### 💻 Code

```java
class SquareCalculator {
    int num;

    void calculateSquare() {
        int square = num * num;
        System.out.println("Square = " + square);
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        SquareCalculator s = new SquareCalculator();
        s.num = 6;
        s.calculateSquare();
    }
}
```

### 📤 Output

```text
Square = 36
```

### 🧠 Memory Trick

Square means multiply **two copies** of the same number.

