# 🎯 Important Java Interview Tips

## Instance Variable vs Local Variable

| Instance variable | Local variable |
|---|---|
| Declared inside a class, outside methods | Declared inside a method or block |
| Belongs to an object | Exists within its declaring scope |
| Gets a default value if not explicitly initialized | Must be initialized before it is read |
| Example: `int age;` | Example: `int sum = a + b;` |

## Constructor vs Method

| Constructor | Method |
|---|---|
| Initializes a new object | Performs an operation |
| Name must match the class name | Can have any valid method name |
| Has no return type | Has a return type, such as `void` or `int` |
| Called during object creation | Called explicitly, or through other program execution |

## Common Mistakes to Avoid

1. Using `void` before a constructor name.
2. Using different names in a method definition and method call.
3. Confusing `name` with `Name` — Java is case-sensitive.
4. Trying to access a local variable from another method.
5. Forgetting to initialize an instance variable with the required input before using it.

